<title>POLAND: Bytom dives on poor November earnings.</title>
<headline>Bytom dives on poor November earnings.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish garment maker Bytom SA fell 9.9 percent to 31.8 zlotys in 730,000-zloty trade after it showed a November loss of 140,000 zlotys, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;They had a bad month but it doesn't mean the firm is in a bad financial situation,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>Traders said Wednesday's bourse approval for the listing of 250,000 Bytom shares, which sold at 27 zlotys in an undersubscribed October offer, also likely hurt the stock.</p>
<p>Some traders said the strong selling after price fixing signalled another fall on Friday.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
